uestion** (Miller 2017). It refers to some kind of \"meaningfulness\".\n","\t- And it is a \"rabbit-hole\" on its own in the [philosophy of science literature](https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/scientific-explanation/)...\n","- For now, let's just say that, in contrast to interpretations, good explanations are:\n","\t- **Contrastive/Counterfactual** – focus on addressing *why this prediction was made instead of another prediction.*\n","\t- **Causal** – can reveal the cause-and-effect relationships that led to the prediction, highlighting the factors that had the greatest impact on the outcome. (Although there are lots of debates on whether all good explanations need to really be causal).\n","\t- **Selective** – emphasize specific aspects of the model or data that are relevant to the *context and previous beliefs* of the explainee. This means they adapt to the explainee’s understanding and focus only on the most pertinent factors, avoiding overwhelming detail.\n","\n","- [Juan M. Durán has an in-depth paper](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0004370221000497) on what a \"*bona fide* explanation\" in AI would have to look like (and we are still not there).\n","\n","- One interesting way to approach explanation is consider that explanations are **meaningful in different aspects**.\n","\t- Christian philosopher Herman Dooyeweerd suggested 15 aspects through which we can interpret things:\n","\n","| **Aspect**          | **Kernel Meaning**                           | **Answer to \"Why is it raining?\"**                                                                                     |\n","|----------------------|----------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n","| **Numerical**        | Discrete quantity                           | \"It’s raining because 20 mm of precipitation is falling today.\"                                                       |\n","| **Spatial**          | Continuous extension                        | \"It’s raining because a large area of the atmosphere is saturated with moisture.\"                                      |\n","| **Kinematic**        | Movement                                     | \"It’s raining because water droplets are falling due to gravity.\"                                                     |\n","| **Physical**         | Energy and causality                        | \"It’s raining because water vapor has condensed into droplets due to cooling.\"                                         |\n","| **Biotic**           | Life and organic growth                     | \"It’s raining to nourish ecosystems and sustain plant and animal life.\"                                                |\n","| **Sensitive**        | Feeling and perception                      | \"It’s raining, and we can feel the cool drops on our skin or hear them tapping on the roof.\"                           |\n","| **Analytical**       | Distinction and clarity                     | \"It’s raining because this weather phenomenon involves liquid water falling from clouds, distinct from snow or hail.\"  |\n","| **Formative**        | Shaping, planning, and control              | \"It’s raining because of seasonal climatic patterns shaped by atmospheric dynamics.\"                                   |\n","| **Lingual**          | Symbolic communication                      | \"It’s raining because the weather forecast predicted precipitation from a cold front.\"                                 |\n","| **Social**           | Social interaction and institutions         | \"It’s raining because natural processes create conditions we must collectively adapt to, like sharing umbrellas.\"      |\n","| **Economic**         | Frugality and stewardship                   | \"It’s raining to replenish water resources, which we must use wisely.\"                                                |\n","| **Aesthetic**        | Harmony and beauty                          | \"It’s raining to create a beautiful rhythm of life and add a sense of calm to the environment.\"                        |\n","| **Juridical**        | Justice and fairness                        | \"It’s raining to ensure equitable distribution of water in this region, benefiting all communities.\"                   |\n","| **Ethical**          | Self-giving love and care                   | \"It’s raining to provide water, a vital resource that sustains life and shows care for creation.\"                      |\n","| **Pistic**           | Faith and ultimate commitment               | \"It’s raining because it is part of God’s provision for the Earth, fulfilling His purpose.\"                            |"],"metadata":{"id":"yN7G24LkUy-J"}}]}